It is Sunday morning.
The sun is shining in through the window in my apartment.
I go out into the kitchen.
I make a pot of fresh coffee.
The smell of coffee is fantastic this morning.
I have a calendar on the wall.
I turn the page to the next month.
It is July now.
I moved to Copenhagen in January.
I came here exactly six months ago.
Time really goes fast.
My first day in this city was very cold.
But today the weather is warm and beautiful.
I want to celebrate this little anniversary.
I have no fixed plans today.
I take my coffee cup and look out over the street.
I want to go out and explore the city at my own pace.
I look forward to enjoying these bright hours.
